you recently signed into your Google Account on your Apple iPhone device.  \r\nIf you do not wish to receive emails to help you set up your device with  \r\nGoogle when you sign into your account on the device for the first time,  \r\nplease unsubscribe  \r\n.\r\n\r\n© 2026 Google LLC 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043","replies":[],"subject":"✅ Dumalnext, finish setting up your Apple iPhone with Google","category":"other","priority":"medium","createdAt":"2026-10-24T15:56:15.064Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-24T15:56:15.064Z","gradeLevel":"Grade 7","studentName":"Google","ticketNumber":"DNHS-CON-69265","contactNumber":""},{"id":"con_1792857372702_0fb77","lrn":"","email":"welcome@supabase.com","source":"inbound_email","status":"PENDING","message":"Everything we announced at Select, and everything else that happened in the last month at Supabase\r\n\r\nSupabase\r\n\r\n********************************\r\nSupabase Update — October 2026\r\n********************************\r\n\r\nHey there 👋,\r\n\r\nHere’s everything that happened with Supabase in the last month:\r\n\r\nBuild anything: Supabase from code, and an MCP server for your app\r\n\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nBuild anything: Supabase from code, and an MCP server for your app\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nYour agent can now set up your backend from code, test changes locally, and deploy your web app and services next to your database.\r\n\r\nRead the blog → ( https://supabase.com/blog/select-2026-build-anything )\r\n\r\nOperate with confidence\r\n\r\n-----------------------\r\nOperate with confidence\r\n-----------------------\r\n\r\nNew data, tools, and controls give your agent what it needs to observe your project, investigate issues, and propose fixes on its own. Pipelines now stream your Postgres data to BigQuery, ClickHouse, DuckLake, and Snowflake in public alpha.\r\n\r\nRead the blog → ( https://supabase.com/blog/select-2026-operate-with-confidence )\r\n\r\nScale without limits: Multigres, OrioleDB, and dbarena\r\n\r\n------------------------------------------------------\r\nScale without limits: Multigres, OrioleDB, and dbarena\r\n------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nMultigres brings high availability and connection pooling to Postgres in private alpha, and OrioleDB, a high-performance storage engine, is now in Public Beta. DBARENA publishes open benchmarks that compare managed Postgres providers.\r\n\r\nRead the blog → ( https://supabase.com/blog/select-2026-scale-without-limits )\r\n\r\nSupabase is acquiring Turso\r\n\r\n---------------------------\r\nSupabase is acquiring Turso\r\n---------------------------\r\n\r\nTurso''s multi-tenant SQLite platform lets an agent create a database as easily as creating a file, with on-demand provisioning and no dedicated machine required. Turso''s Glauber Costa and Pekka Enberg join Supabase to build the infrastructure agentic workloads need, and existing Supabase and Turso databases keep running exactly as they do today.\r\n\r\nRead the blog → ( https://supabase.com/blog/supabase-is-acquiring-turso )\r\n\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n---------------------------\r\nQuick Product Announcements\r\n---------------------------\r\n\r\n* Supabase is now a connector in Gemini Enterprise, so you can query your projects and take action in natural language next to GitHub, Linear, and Jira. [Blog ( https://supabase.com/blog/supabase-is-now-available-in-gemini-enterprise )]\r\n* Logs move to usage-based pricing for ingest and query scanning, with more than 90% of projects inside the included limits and no charges until early 2027. [Changelog ( https://supabase.com/changelog/logs-usage-based-pricing )]\r\n\r\n------------------\r\nMade with Supabase\r\n------------------\r\n\r\n* Ekwo OS - open-source double-entry accounting for 90+ countries that installs onto your own Supabase project as Postgres migrations. [GitHub ( https://github.com/Ekwo-ai/ekwo-os )] [Website ( https://ekwo.ai )]\r\n* Atomic CRM 1.6 - marmelab''s open-source CRM now ships a built-in MCP server that runs as an Edge Function with OAuth. [GitHub ( https://github.com/marmelab/atomic-crm )]\r\n* Supabuckt - an open-source Storage browser for Android and iOS, built with Kotlin Multiplatform, that switches between your projects. [GitHub ( https://github.com/hieuwu/supabase-storage-client )] [Website ( https://apps.apple.com/us/app/supabuckt-supabase-storage/id6759938222 )]\r\n* NO SUS - a student privacy toolkit with burn-after-read encrypted notes and watermarked file sharing, built on Flutter and Supabase. [Website ( https://nosus.foo )]\r\n\r\n--------------------\r\nCommunity Highlights\r\n--------------------\r\n\r\n* How I''d Launch a Dating App From Zero: Supabase Growth Strategy. [Video ( https://youtube.com/watch?v=xP8JEnWzGEA )]\r\n* Why MCP is the key to building with Supabase, from Stripe Developers. [Video ( https://youtube.com/watch?v=6pIiR7-TbJo )]\r\n* Supabase Is Quietly Becoming a Data Platform. [Video ( https://youtube.com/watch?v=0RYFbRxXDv8 )]\r\n* supabase-audit runs 11 read-only checks for RLS, exposure, and performance footguns from one SQL file. [GitHub ( https://github.com/Concepto505/supabase-audit )]\r\n* Six Multiplayer Browser Games on Cloudflare Workers and Supabase: What Broke. [Blog ( https://dev.to/board_it_b11ff7d58bf863f8/six-multiplayer-browser-games-on-cloudflare-workers-and-supabase-what-broke-5244 )]\r\n\r\n------------\r\nWe''re Hiring\r\n------------\r\n\r\nCome join one of the fastest-growing open source projects ever 🤗\r\n\r\nHere are the jobs of the month:\r\n\r\n* Partnerships Manager, Ecosystem ( https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/supabase/f0f277ac-b96c-478a-81ca-7bd80612533f )\r\n* Developer Relations Engineer ( https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/supabase/98ae5c78-eab7-4879-b143-96b98e4d0dbb )\r\n* Platform Engineer - Compute Capacity ( https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/supabase/4eb14408-51e6-4c58-812a-3782d5c0b045 )\r\n\r\n----------------------------------\r\n⚠️ Baking hot meme zone ⚠️\r\n----------------------------------\r\n\r\nMeme of the month ( https://x.com/supabase/status/2105022757121790184 )\r\n\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n©2026 Supabase Inc.\r\n3500 S. DuPont Highway, Kent 19901, Dover, Delaware, USA\r\n\r\nThe email was sent to dumalnext@gmail.com. To no longer receive these emails, unsubscribe ( https://track.customer.io/unsubscribe/dgSFuAsDAKXRtQak0bUGAaE2dRKq73uzIFHXWROctg== ) here.","replies":[],"subject":"Supa Update October 2026","category":"other","priority":"medium","createdAt":"2026-10-24T15:56:12.702Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-24T15:56:12.702Z","gradeLevel":"Grade 7","studentName":"Supabase","ticketNumber":"DNHS-CON-92204","contactNumber":""},{"id":"con_1792857369321_sr0oy","lrn":"","email":"no-reply@accounts.google.com","source":"inbound_email","status":"PENDING","message":"[image: Google]\r\nA new sign-in on Apple iPhone\r\n\r\n\r\ndumalnext@gmail.com\r\nWe noticed a new sign-in to your Google Account on a Apple iPhone device.\r\nIf this was you, you don’t need to do anything. If not, we’ll help you\r\nsecure your account.\r\nCheck activity\r\n\r\nYou can also see security activity at\r\nhttps://myaccount.google.com/notifications\r\nYou received this email to let you know about important changes to your\r\nGoogle Account and services.\r\n© 2026 Google LLC, 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA","replies":[],"subject":"Security alert","category":"other","priority":"medium","createdAt":"2026-10-24T15:56:09.321Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-24T15:56:09.321Z","gradeLevel":"Grade 7","studentName":"Google","ticketNumber":"DNHS-CON-72066","contactNumber":""},{"id":"con_1792857366264_88t5g","lrn":"","email":"no-reply@google.com","source":"inbound_email","status":"PENDING","message":"Dumalnext, you''re almost done setting Google up on your Windows\r\n\r\n\r\nTake a minute to set up Google apps & settings on your new device\r\n\r\nFinish setup  \r\n\r\n\r\nThis email was sent to dumalnex