,"createdAt":"2026-10-24T15:55:48.174Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-24T15:55:48.174Z","gradeLevel":"Grade 7","studentName":"Vercel","ticketNumber":"DNHS-CON-91589","contactNumber":""},{"id":"con_1792857345052_z7dny","lrn":"","email":"noreply@supabase.com","source":"inbound_email","status":"PENDING","message":"10 days left: new tables in \"public\" need explicit grants from October 30.\r\n\r\nHi there,\r\n\r\nOn October 30, ten days from now, Supabase will stop automatically granting Data API access to new tables in the \"public\" schema for existing projects.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nYour existing tables are not affected. They keep their current grants and stay accessible through the Data API.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nWhat changes on October 30\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nAny table created in \"public\" from that date onwards needs an explicit GRANT before supabase-js, PostgREST, or GraphQL can reach it. Without one, the API returns a \"permission denied\" error that includes the statement to run.\r\n\r\nThis includes migrations that recreate your schema: new projects, preview branches, and local \"supabase db reset\".\r\n\r\nWhat to do\r\n\r\nAdd grants in the same migration that creates each table:\r\n\r\ngrant select\r\n\r\non public.your_table\r\n\r\nto anon;\r\n\r\ngrant select, insert, update, delete\r\n\r\non public.your_table\r\n\r\nto authenticated;\r\n\r\ngrant select, insert, update, delete\r\n\r\non public.your_table\r\n\r\nto service_role;\r\n\r\nCheck which tables are exposed in your project''s Data API settings ( https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/_/integrations/data_api/settings ).\r\n\r\nLearn more about this change ( https://github.com/orgs/supabase/discussions/45329 )\r\n\r\nIf you have any questions, please reach out to our support team ( https://supabase.com/dashboard/support/new?subject=Breaking%20Change%20-%20Data%20API%20Exposure ).\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe team at Supabase\r\n\r\nX ( https://x.com/supabase ) Custom ( https://github.com/supabase ) Custom ( https://discord.supabas